{"surah": 95, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "وَٱلتِّينِ وَٱلزَّيْتُونِ ", "translation": "By the fig and the olive[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلتِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّtlٱَw", "root": "تين"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَٱلزَّيْتُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُtْyَّzlٱَw", "root": "زيت"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَطُورِ سِينِينَ ", "translation": "And [by] Mount Sinai", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَطُورِ", "translit": "ِrwُṭَw", "root": "طور"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سِينِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnyِs", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَهَٰذَا ٱلْبَلَدِ ٱلْأَمِينِ ", "translation": "And [by] this secure city [i.e., Makkah],", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَهَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْبَلَدِ", "translit": "ِdَlَbْlٱ", "root": "بلد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْأَمِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِmَaʾْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "لَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ فِىٓ أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ ", "translation": "We have certainly created man in the best of stature;[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "خَلَقْنَا", "translit": "āَnْqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَحْسَنِ", "translit": "ِnَsْḥَaʾ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَقْوِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِwْqَt", "root": "قوم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "ثُمَّ رَدَدْنَٰهُ أَسْفَلَ سَٰفِلِينَ ", "translation": "Then We return him to the lowest of the low,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَدَدْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْdَdَr", "root": "ردد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَسْفَلَ", "translit": "َlَfْsَaʾ", "root": "سفل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَٰفِلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlِfَٰs", "root": "سفل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ فَلَهُمْ أَجْرٌ غَيْرُ مَمْنُونٍ ", "translation": "Except for those who believe and do righteous deeds, for they will have a reward uninterrupted.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿعَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَجْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "غَيْرُ", "translit": "ُrْyَغ", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَمْنُونٍ", "translit": "ٍnwُnْmَm", "root": "منن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "فَمَا يُكَذِّبُكَ بَعْدُ بِٱلدِّينِ ", "translation": "So what yet causes you to deny the Recompense?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَمَا", "translit": "āَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُكَذِّبُكَ", "translit": "َkُbِّhdَkُy", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بَعْدُ", "translit": "ُdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱِb", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "أَلَيْسَ ٱللَّهُ بِأَحْكَمِ ٱلْحَٰكِمِينَ ", "translation": "Is not Allāh the most just of judges?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَيْسَ", "translit": "َsْyَlَaʾ", "root": "ليس"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِأَحْكَمِ", "translit": "ِmَkْḥَaʾِb", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْحَٰكِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِkَٰḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"4": [{"arabic": "وَكَذَلِكَ خَلَقَ اللهُ سُبْحَانَهُ الْخَلْقَ وَهُمْ فِي ابْتِدَاءِ فِطْرَتِهِمْ يَحْتَاجُونَ إِلَى اسْتِعْمَالِ الشَّهَوَاتِ لِتُكْمَلَ بِهَا أَبْدَانُهُمْ فَيَبْعُدُونَ بِهَا عَنْ حَضْرَتِهِ وَإِنَّمَا سَعَادَتُهُمْ فِي الْقُرْبِ مِنْهُ فَأَعْدَلَهُمْ مِنَ النِّعَمِ مَا يَقْدِرُونَ عَلَى اسْتِعْمَالِهِ فِي نَيْلِ دَرَجَةِ الْقُرْبِ وَعَنْ بُعْدِهِمْ وَقُرْبِهِمْ عَبَّرَ اللهُ تَعَالَى إِذْ قَالَ: ﴿ لَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْإِنْسَانَ فِي أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ ثُمَّ رَدَدْنَاهُ أَسْفَلَ سَافِلِينَ إِلَّ", "english": "And similarly, Allah (the Exalted) created the creation, and they in the beginning of their innate disposition (Fitrah) need to use the desires (Shahawat) to perfect their bodies with them, so they distance themselves with them from His presence (Hudur). And indeed their happiness (Sa'adah) is in proximity (Qurb) to Him. So He provided them with the blessings (Ni'am) that they are capable of using to attain the degree of proximity. And concerning their distance and proximity, Allah (the Exalted) expressed when He said: 'Indeed, We created the human being (Al-Insan) in the best form (Ahsan Taqwim), then We return him to the lowest of the low (Asfal Safilin), except those who believe.' Therefore, the blessings (Ni'am) of Allah (the Exalted) are instruments (Alat) by which the servant (Abd) ascends from the lowest of the low. Allah (the Exalted) created them for the sake of the servant so that he may attain with them the happiness (Sa'adah) of proximity (Qurb). And Allah (the Exalted) is independent of him, whether proximity or distance. And the servant (Abd) in them is between using them in obedience (Taa'ah), so he would have given thanks (Shakar) for conforming to the love (Mahabbah) of his Master (Mawla), and between using them in his disobedience (Ma'siyah), so he has disbelieved (Kafar) for plunging into what his Master (Mawla) dislikes and does not approve for him. For indeed Allah does not approve for His servants disbelief (Kufr) and disobedience (Ma'siyah). And if he neglects them and does not use them in obedience (Taa'ah) nor disobedience (Ma'siyah), then it is also disbelief (Kufr), a denial (Kufran) of the blessing (Ni'mah) through waste. And everything created in the world is only created as an instrument (Alah) for the servant (Abd) so that he may connect with it to the happiness (Sa'adah) of the Hereafter and attainment of proximity (Qurb) from Allah (the Exalted). So every obedient one (Muti') is, according to his obedience (Taa'ah), giving thanks (Shakir) for the blessing (Ni'mah) of Allah in the means (Asbab) which he used in obedience (Taa'ah). And every lazy one (Kaslan) who abandoned the use or disobedient one (Asi) who used them in the way of distance (B'ud) is a disbeliever (Kafir) straying in other than the love (Mahabbah) of Allah (the Exalted). So disobedience (Ma'siyah) and obedience (Taa'ah) encompass them both the will (Mashiyyah), but they do not encompass them both the love (Mahabbah) and dislike (Karaha). Rather, perhaps a desired thing (Murad) is beloved (Mahbub) and perhaps a desired thing (Murad) is disliked (Makruh).", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "General"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 250, 1495], [2, 1495, 3182]], "2": [[1, 250, 1492], [2, 1492, 2921]], "3": [[1, 250, 1333], [2, 1333, 2159], [3, 2159, 3312]], "4": [[1, 400, 1222], [2, 1222, 2699], [3, 2699, 4190], [4, 4190, 5357], [5, 5357, 6405], [6, 6405, 7952]], "5": [[1, 350, 1231], [2, 1231, 2658], [3, 2658, 3725], [4, 3725, 5278]], "6": [[1, 400, 1254], [2, 1254, 2315], [3, 2315, 3723], [4, 3723, 5188], [5, 5188, 6822], [6, 6822, 7554], [7, 7554, 8202], [8, 8202, 8878], [9, 8878, 9911]], "7": [[1, 350, 1100], [2, 1100, 2438], [3, 2438, 3105], [4, 3105, 4469]], "8": [[1, 350, 1311], [2, 1311, 2102], [3, 2102, 3163], [4, 3163, 4678]]}, "husary": {"1": [[1, 350, 2642], [2, 2642, 5746]], "2": [[1, 350, 2337], [2, 2337, 4623]], "3": [[1, 350, 2324], [2, 2324, 3829], [3, 3829, 5929]], "4": [[1, 400, 1704], [2, 1704, 4048],